          "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a functor between categories.\nWe say <TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0002> is cofinal in <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> or that\n<MATH_0004> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>cofinal<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> for all <MATH_0005> there exist an\n<MATH_0006> and a morphism <MATH_0007>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> given <MATH_0008>, <MATH_0009>\nand morphisms <MATH_0010> and <MATH_0011> there exist a sequence\nof morphisms\n<MATH_0012>\nin <MATH_0013> and morphisms <MATH_0014> in <MATH_0015>\nwith <MATH_0016> and <MATH_0017> the given morphisms\nsuch that the diagrams\n<MATH_0018>\ncommute for <MATH_0019>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nIn other words, fixing an object <MATH_0020> of <MATH_0021> consider the\nset <MATH_0022> of pairs <MATH_0023> where <MATH_0024> is an object of <MATH_0025> and\n<MATH_0026> is a morphism. Consider the equivalence relation\non <MATH_0027> generated by <MATH_0028> if there exists a\nmorphism <MATH_0029> with <MATH_0030>. Then <MATH_0031> should\nconsist of exactly one equivalence class.\n",
          "source_text_hash": "sha256:d81785c87704f5eb0dc9f1b6274da51c82fe5fd1b08aa51b820f5c98d9208b35",
